gate: OPEN
v:4 c:$ m:navitrack-config role:dev x:qa
task: S17 T3 — Manual smoke: live Navitrack BLE scan/connect/read
sprint: S17
requires: [QA, FRONTEND_DEV, MOBILE_TAURI]
test_mandate: ../intel/TEST-COVERAGE-MANDATE.md
quality_mandate: ../intel/CODE-QUALITY-MANDATE.md

context: |
  Physical DUT on hand = Navitrack BLE (intel/NAVITRACK-BLE-DUT.md). Follow DEVICE-QA macOS path:
  BT on → permission → scan (name filters) → connect → password 0x50 → Standard read chain → live telemetry if available.
  Record results in sprints/S17/SMOKE-NOTES.md (DUT name seen, OS version, pass/fail, blockers).
  If protocol/GATT mismatch: file follow-up .pd — do not silently change invariants without T0/decision.
  Package manager: bun. No live BLE in unit tests.

out:
  - sprints/S17/SMOKE-NOTES.md
  - DEVICE-QA.md checkboxes updated / linked
  - follow-up .pd only if defects found

cmd:
  - bun run test

done:
  - SMOKE-NOTES records macOS session vs live DUT
  - Happy path pass OR explicit fail + next task proposals
  - `bun run test` still green
